        'After the embryo implants, your body starts making the pregnancy hormone hCG, and rising hormones can trigger subtle changes even before your period is due. These signs are easy to confuse with the ordinary run-up to a period, though, because they overlap so much. That is why symptoms alone cannot confirm pregnancy; only a test can.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'If you are hoping to know early, it is fine to notice these signs, but try not to read too much into them either way. The clearest step is a home test from the first day of your missed period, using first morning urine, and testing again in a few days if it is negative but your period still has not come.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'See your doctor to confirm a positive test and start care; there is no need to see one just for early symptoms.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Symptom-spotting in the two-week wait can be all-consuming; whether you feel everything or nothing, only a test gives a real answer, so be gentle with yourself while you wait.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Some early signs can appear before a missed period.',
        'Tender breasts, fatigue, mild cramps, smell sensitivity.',
        'They overlap heavily with normal pre-period symptoms.',
        'Symptoms cannot confirm pregnancy; only a test can.',
        'Test from your missed period, using morning urine.',
      ]),
    ],
