  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-GEN-003',
    number: 20,
    month: 1,
    question: 'When is it safe to tell people I\'m pregnant?',
    category: 'General (Emotional)',
    applicability: 'First trimester',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No (handled gently)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'There is no medically fixed rule for when to tell people you are pregnant. Many families in India wait until after the first three months, when the chance of miscarriage has dropped, but the timing is entirely your personal choice.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'The custom of waiting until around 12 to 13 weeks exists because most miscarriages happen in the first trimester, so by the end of it the pregnancy feels more settled to many parents. That said, some people share early precisely so they have support if anything goes wrong, while others prefer privacy. Neither choice is right or wrong; it is about what feels comfortable for you and your partner.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'You might think about who you would want beside you in both the good news and any hard moments, and let that guide who you tell and when. There is no need to follow a timeline set by anyone else, including family expectations, if a different choice feels better for you.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'This is a personal decision rather than a medical one, so there is no need to ask your doctor, though you can if it helps.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'The "wait until twelve weeks" custom can feel like a rule, but it is really just one option; the right time to share is whenever you feel ready.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'There is no medical rule on when to announce.',
        'Many wait past the first three months as miscarriage risk falls.',
        'Some share early for support, others prefer privacy.',
        'The choice is yours and your partner\'s.',
        'Family custom need not decide it for you.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-CANI-EAT-011',
      'PREG-GEN-001',
      'PREG-GEN-002',
