  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-BABY-002',
    number: 21,
    month: 1,
    question: 'When does my baby\'s heart start beating?',
    category: 'Baby Development',
    applicability: 'Weeks 5 to 7',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Your baby\'s heart begins to beat very early, at around 5 to 6 weeks of pregnancy, though it usually cannot be seen on a scan until about 6 to 7 weeks. Early on the rate is slower, then it speeds up over the following weeks.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'In the first weeks a tiny heart tube forms and starts to pulse, even before the heart is fully built, pushing blood to the growing embryo. At around 6 to 7 weeks the rate is often 90 to 110 bpm (beats per minute), rising to about 140 to 170 by 9 weeks, then settling into a steady range. This early flicker is one of the first signs a pregnancy is progressing well.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'If your first scan is a little early, the heartbeat may not be visible yet, and your doctor will usually simply arrange a repeat scan a week or two later. This is common and does not by itself mean something is wrong; often the dates were just slightly off.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Your doctor will advise a follow-up scan if it is too early to see the heartbeat, and will guide you from there.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Seeing or hearing that first heartbeat is one of pregnancy\'s most moving moments, and it usually arrives a little later than parents expect.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'The heart starts beating around 5 to 6 weeks.',
        'It is usually visible on a scan around 6 to 7 weeks.',
        'The early rate is slower, then speeds up.',
        'Not seeing it at a very early scan is often just timing.',
        'A repeat scan is common and reassuring.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-SCAN-020',
