  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-CANI-TAKE-002',
    number: 22,
    month: 1,
    question: 'I took a medicine before I knew I was pregnant. Which medicines are safe?',
    category: 'Medicines (Can I > Take)',
    applicability: 'All trimesters',
    canI: 'Take',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'If you took a common medicine before you knew you were pregnant, try not to worry, as most everyday medicines cause no harm, especially early on. Going forward, the safest approach is not to take or stop any medicine without checking first with your doctor or pharmacist.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Many medicines are safe in pregnancy, a smaller number are not, and quite a few sit in between and need a doctor\'s judgement. Rather than deciding for yourself which is which, the reliable rule is to ask before taking anything, including over-the-counter and herbal products. Importantly, you should not stop a prescribed medicine, for conditions like thyroid, diabetes, epilepsy or mental health, on your own, since not treating these can be more harmful than the medicine.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Keep a note of anything you take, and check with your doctor or pharmacist before starting or stopping it. If you took something before realising you were pregnant, mention it at your first visit so your doctor can reassure you or adjust as needed.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Always check with your doctor or pharmacist before starting or stopping any medicine, and mention anything you took before you knew.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'A single dose of a common medicine before you knew rarely causes harm, so the useful response is a calm check rather than worry.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Most everyday medicines taken before you knew cause no harm.',
        'Do not start any medicine, including over-the-counter or herbal, without checking first.',
        'Never stop a prescribed medicine on your own.',
        'Keep a note of what you take.',
        'Mention anything you took before you knew at your first visit.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-CANI-EAT-001',
      'PREG-SCAN-021',
      'PREG-BODY-004',
