  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-BODY-005',
    number: 23,
    month: 1,
    question: 'Why am I so tired in early pregnancy?',
    category: 'Symptoms',
    applicability: 'First trimester',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Feeling very tired in early pregnancy is extremely common and usually harmless. It is largely driven by the rise in the hormone progesterone, and for most women it eases as the first trimester ends.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'In the early weeks your body is working hard, building the placenta and increasing blood volume, while progesterone rises sharply and has a naturally sleepy effect. This combination can leave you drained even before there is any bump to show for it. The tiredness often lifts in the second trimester, though it can return later on.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'The most helpful response is to rest without guilt: short naps, an earlier bedtime, and letting some things wait. Gentle activity, staying hydrated, and regular balanced meals can also help your energy. Because anaemia can worsen tiredness, this is worth mentioning at your antenatal visit.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Mention it to your doctor if the tiredness feels extreme or comes with breathlessness or dizziness, as anaemia is common and easily treated.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Early pregnancy tiredness is real and often underestimated; treating rest as necessary rather than indulgent usually helps most.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Extreme tiredness is common and usually harmless.',
        'It is driven mainly by rising progesterone.',
        'It often eases in the second trimester.',
        'Rest, gentle activity and good meals help.',
        'Mention it if severe, as anaemia can be a cause.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
