  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-BODY-006',
    number: 24,
    month: 1,
    question: 'Is constipation and bloating normal in early pregnancy?',
    category: 'Body & Symptoms',
    applicability: 'All trimesters',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Constipation and bloating are very common in early pregnancy and are usually nothing to worry about. Pregnancy hormones slow the gut down, and iron in prenatal supplements can add to it.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'The hormone progesterone relaxes the muscles of your digestive tract, so food moves through more slowly, which can leave you feeling bloated, gassy or blocked up. The extra iron in many pregnancy supplements can make constipation firmer. This is a normal adjustment, not a sign anything is wrong.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Simple steps usually help a lot: plenty of fibre from fruits, vegetables and whole grains, drinking enough water through the day, and staying gently active. In an Indian kitchen, foods like soaked overnight raisins, plenty of dal, vegetables and whole grains can be useful. If iron seems to be the culprit, your doctor can advise.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor before taking any laxative, and mention constipation that is severe, painful, or comes with bleeding.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'It is an unglamorous side of early pregnancy that few talk about, yet small daily habits usually ease it more than any quick fix.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Constipation and bloating are common and usually harmless.',
        'Caused by hormones slowing the gut, plus iron supplements.',
        'Fibre, water and gentle movement help.',
        'Ask before using laxatives.',
        'Tell your doctor if it is severe or painful.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-CANI-DRINK-003',
      'PREG-CANI-EAT-001',
      'PREG-BODY-005',
    ],
  ),
