  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-BODY-008',
    number: 26,
    month: 1,
    question: 'Why do I have food cravings and aversions?',
    category: 'Body & Symptoms',
    applicability: 'First trimester',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Sudden food cravings and strong dislikes are a very normal part of early pregnancy. They are driven by shifting hormones and a heightened sense of smell, and they usually settle as pregnancy goes on.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Rising pregnancy hormones can change how food tastes and smells, so a dish you loved may suddenly turn your stomach, while you crave something you rarely ate. A sharpened sense of smell adds to this. It is harmless, and there is no need to explain or resist every craving or aversion.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'The practical aim is balance, not perfection: follow reasonable cravings in moderation, and work around aversions by finding other foods that give similar nutrition. If cooking smells trigger you, a fan or asking someone else to cook can help. One thing to mention to your doctor is any craving for non-food items like chalk or mud, which can signal a deficiency.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Tell your doctor if you crave non-food items such as chalk, ash or mud, as this can point to a deficiency worth checking.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Cravings and aversions can feel odd and even inconvenient, but they are a normal quirk of early pregnancy rather than something to manage strictly.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Cravings and aversions are normal in early pregnancy.',
        'Caused by hormones and a heightened sense of smell.',
        'Follow cravings in moderation; work around aversions.',
        'Use a fan or ask for help if cooking smells trigger you.',
        'Tell your doctor about cravings for non-food items.',
      ]),
    ],
