    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Feeling dizzy or lightheaded is common in early pregnancy and usually harmless. It mostly happens because pregnancy hormones relax your blood vessels and slightly lower your blood pressure.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'As progesterone rises, your blood vessels widen and blood pressure can dip, so standing up quickly may briefly reduce blood flow to your brain. Going too long without eating can lower blood sugar, and heat or dehydration can make it worse. Anemia, which is common in India, can also contribute, which is one more reason it is checked early.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Stand up slowly, eat small regular meals, stay well hydrated, avoid long spells of standing, and wear loose, comfortable clothing. Sitting or lying down at the first wave of dizziness, then getting up gently, usually settles it. If it keeps happening, mention it, as your iron levels are worth checking.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'See your doctor if you actually faint, or if dizziness comes with bleeding, severe headache or one-sided tummy pain, so it can be checked.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Occasional lightheadedness is a normal part of your body recalibrating, and a few simple habits usually keep it in check.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Dizziness is common and usually harmless early on.',
        'Caused by lower blood pressure, low blood sugar, heat or dehydration.',
        'Anemia can contribute.',
        'Rise slowly, eat regularly, hydrate, avoid long standing.',
        'See your doctor if you faint or have bleeding with it.',
