  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-BODY-013',
    number: 41,
    month: 1,
    question: 'Implantation bleeding vs a period: how do I tell the difference?',
    category: 'Body & Symptoms',
    applicability: 'Month 1',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Implantation bleeding is light pink or brown spotting that some women notice when the embryo settles into the womb, usually around the time a period is due. The easiest way to tell it from a period is that it stays much lighter and shorter and never builds into a full flow.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'When the fertilised egg burrows into the womb lining, it can disturb tiny blood vessels and release a little old blood, which is why it often looks pink or brown rather than bright red. It happens in roughly one in four pregnancies, and many women never have it at all. A period, by contrast, starts light and gets heavier over days, is bright or dark red, often has clots, and comes with stronger cramps.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'A few clues help: implantation spotting is light enough for just a panty liner, lasts from a few hours to two or three days, and brings only mild cramps, while a period soaks pads and lasts longer. Because it happens before your hormone levels are high, a pregnancy test may be too early to be reliable during the spotting itself, so testing from the day of your missed period gives a clearer answer.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'See your doctor if bleeding is heavy, soaks pads, has clots, or comes with severe or one-sided pain, so it can be checked.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'The two-week wait makes every spot feel loaded with meaning; a light, brief spot before your period is often nothing to worry about, though only a test can confirm what it means.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Implantation bleeding is light pink or brown spotting.',
        'It is lighter and shorter than a period, with no clots.',
        'About 1 in 4 women have it, and many do not.',
        'Test from your missed period, not during the spotting.',
        'Get heavy bleeding or pain checked.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-HEALTH-001',
      'PREG-TEST-001',
      'PREG-BODY-014',
    ],
  ),
  PregFaq(
