      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'In the early weeks, brown spotting can come from implantation, from a little old blood clearing, or from the cervix being more sensitive and richly supplied with blood, so it may spot slightly after sex or an internal examination. Because it is old blood, it tends to be light and to look pink-brown or rusty. It is usually not a sign of a problem.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Light brown discharge that comes and goes, without pain or a foul smell, generally just needs a panty liner and a note of when it happens. What is worth attention is brown discharge that turns into fresh red bleeding, becomes heavy, or comes with cramping, pain or a bad smell.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Contact your doctor if the discharge becomes red and heavy, or comes with cramping, pain or a foul smell, so it can be checked.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Brown discharge looks alarming precisely because it is discoloured, but old blood leaving gently is usually the least worrying kind.',
