  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-EMOTION-003',
    number: 43,
    month: 1,
    question: 'Are mood swings normal in early pregnancy?',
    category: 'Emotional Wellbeing',
    applicability: 'First trimester',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'Yes (mental health, gentle register)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Mood swings are very common in early pregnancy and are a normal response to a surge of hormones and a big life change. Feeling weepy, irritable or up and down, sometimes within the same hour, does not mean anything is wrong.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Rising estrogen and progesterone affect the brain chemicals that influence mood, much as they can before a period, but more intensely. On top of the hormones, tiredness, nausea and the sheer adjustment to being pregnant all add to the emotional ups and downs. For many women these swings are strongest in the first trimester, around weeks six to ten, and ease as the body settles.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'It helps to be gentle with yourself, rest when you can, talk to someone you trust, and let those around you know you may be more sensitive for a while. Mood swings are one thing; if low mood, anxiety or tearfulness becomes constant, heavy, or starts to interfere with daily life, that is worth sharing so you can get support.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Speak to your doctor if low mood or anxiety feels constant, heavy, or is affecting your daily life, so you can get the right support.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Feeling more emotional right now is not a weakness; it is a very human response to one of life\'s biggest changes.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Mood swings are normal in early pregnancy.',
        'Driven by hormones plus tiredness and adjustment.',
        'Often strongest around weeks 6 to 10.',
        'Rest, support and honesty with loved ones help.',
        'Reach out if low mood or anxiety is constant or disruptive.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-EMOTION-001',
      'PREG-BODY-005',
    ],
