    number: 45,
    month: 1,
    question: 'Can I sleep on my back or stomach in early pregnancy?',
    category: 'Lifestyle (Can I > Do)',
    applicability: 'First trimester (guidance shifts later)',
    canI: 'Do',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'In early pregnancy you can sleep in whatever position is comfortable, including on your back or stomach. Your baby is still small and well protected, so there is no need to worry about your sleep position yet.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'In the first trimester the womb is still low in the pelvis and cushioned by muscle and fluid, so lying on your stomach or back does no harm. Later, from around the middle of pregnancy, sleeping flat on your back can let the growing womb press on a major vein and reduce blood flow, which is why side sleeping is advised then, and research links going to sleep on your side in the last trimester with safer outcomes. For now, comfort is the only thing that matters.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Sleep however you rest best. If you like, this is a gentle time to start getting used to sleeping on your side, either side is fine, since you will be encouraged to favour it later. A pillow between your knees or under your bump makes side sleeping comfortable when the time comes, and if you wake on your back later in pregnancy, there is no need to panic, simply roll onto your side.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'From later in pregnancy your doctor will advise going to sleep on your side; ask if you are unsure when to switch.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Early on, good sleep matters far more than the position you get it in, so rest easy.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Any position is fine in early pregnancy, including back and stomach.',
        'The baby is still small and protected.',
        'Side sleeping matters more from around mid-pregnancy.',
        'Either side is fine; a pillow helps you get comfortable.',
        'Don\'t worry about waking on your back later, just roll over.',
      ]),
    ],
