    number: 47,
    month: 1,
    question: 'Can I take hot baths, use a sauna or steam during pregnancy?',
    category: 'Lifestyle (Can I > Do)',
    applicability: 'First trimester (caution highest)',
    canI: 'Do',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'A warm bath is fine in pregnancy, but it is best to avoid getting too hot, and to skip saunas, steam rooms and very hot baths, especially in the first trimester. The concern is overheating, not bathing itself.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Raising your core body temperature too high in early pregnancy, roughly above 39 degrees Celsius, has been linked to a higher risk of neural tube defects, which affect the baby\'s brain and spinal cord as they form in the first weeks. Saunas, steam rooms and very hot water raise body temperature quickly, which is why health bodies advise caution. A comfortably warm bath that does not leave you flushed or dizzy does not carry this risk.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Keep bath water warm rather than hot, so it feels pleasant and not reddening, and keep hot soaks short. Get out if you feel flushed, dizzy or too warm, and drink some water. In hot Indian summers the same idea applies to avoiding overheating in general: stay cool and well hydrated.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Let your doctor know if you have had a high fever in early pregnancy, since that also raises body temperature and is worth reviewing.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'You do not have to give up a relaxing bath, just keep it warm rather than hot, and let comfort be your guide.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Warm baths are fine.',
        'Avoid saunas, steam rooms and very hot baths, especially early on.',
