  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-HEALTH-007',
    number: 48,
    month: 1,
    question: 'What does thyroid in pregnancy mean?',
    category: 'Health & Medical',
    applicability: 'All trimesters (checked Month 1 to 2)',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    held: true,
    heldNote: 'Yes',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'The thyroid, a small gland in your neck, plays a big role in pregnancy, and thyroid problems, especially an underactive thyroid, are common in India. The reassuring part is that they are easily checked with a simple blood test and well managed with treatment.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Pregnancy places extra demand on the thyroid, and in the early weeks your baby relies on your thyroid hormones for brain development before making its own. If the thyroid is underactive (hypothyroidism) and left untreated, particularly early on, it can affect the baby\'s development and raise certain pregnancy risks, which is why a thyroid test, TSH (thyroid-stimulating hormone), is part of early pregnancy blood work. Underactive thyroid is especially common in parts of India.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'If your thyroid test is abnormal, your doctor will start or adjust treatment and monitor your levels through pregnancy; this is routine and effective. If you already have a thyroid condition, tell your doctor as early as possible, as your dose often needs adjusting once you are pregnant. Because thyroid care is specific to you, your doctor guides all medication and dosing.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Tell your doctor early if you have a thyroid condition or a family history, so your levels can be checked and treatment adjusted; your doctor guides all medication.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'A thyroid issue in pregnancy can sound worrying, but it is common, easily found, and very treatable once your doctor is guiding it.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'The thyroid strongly affects pregnancy, and your baby relies on yours early on.',
        'Underactive thyroid is common in India.',
        'It is checked with a TSH blood test early in pregnancy.',
        'Treatment and monitoring manage it well.',
        'Tell your doctor early if you have a thyroid condition.',
      ]),
    ],
